 causing a `ConcurrentModificationException`. The same problem occurs in `removeFromContext()` when it removes items from the list while iterating through it.\n\nThe cleanest solution is to switch to an Iterator in `removeFromContext()` and use `iterator.remove()` to safely modify the collection during iteration. Alternatively, I could use an explicit index-based loop or `removeIf()`, but the Iterator approach is more idiomatic. I'll apply the iterator fix to resolve this.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
