urrent access persists: `getView()` could still be iterating while the listener modifies the list. Since Android's ListView operations run on the UI thread, this is fundamentally a threading concern that needs a more robust solution.\n\nI could copy the context list before iterating in `getView()`, or simplify the loop logic so that `setBackgroundColor()` and `setChecked(true)` only execute for the matching file instead of the last item. The simpler fix is just correcting the loop logic, though copying the list would be the most defensive approach.\n\nNow I'm examining the checkbox handling logic in the code—there's a loop that checks if a file matches items in the context, setting the background and checked state when it finds a match, but the else branch is problematic because it keeps unchecking the box even after finding the right file.\n\nThe real issue is that `removeFromContext` modifies the collection while it's being iterated over, so I need to use an iterator or collect items to remove separately. For the `getView` method, even though the checkbox listener should be safe since the file is already in context, it's better to avoid unnecessary state changes altogether.\n\nI'll stick with fixing just `removeFromContext` since that's where the actual crash is occurring, then run a build to confirm the fix works.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
